# =============================================================================
# NiftyCasino environment
#
# NOTHING here is required for local dev. With no env vars at all the app runs on
# the in-memory store and auth is simply unavailable (the UI shows a banner).
# See README → "Supabase setup (production auth + Postgres)".
#
# Copy to .env and fill in what you need:   cp .env.example .env
# Never commit .env — it is gitignored, and the service role key bypasses RLS.
# =============================================================================

# --- Supabase auth (browser + server session) --------------------------------
# Project URL + anon key: Project Settings → API.
# The anon key is public by design — it only ever sees rows the RLS policies allow.
#
# These two also decide the auth mode (see README → "Auth"):
#   both set  → real Supabase email auth (signup → verify → login)
#   URL unset → dev-auth fallback: pick any handle and you are that player.
# Set them together; a URL without the anon key disables the fallback and leaves
# auth unusable rather than switching modes silently.
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Supabase auth admin (server only) --------------------------------------
# service_role key: Project Settings → API. BYPASSES ROW LEVEL SECURITY.
# Server-only ($lib/server/supabaseAdmin.ts) — used for auth admin calls (create
# user, verification links, delete account). Never expose it to a browser.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Postgres (game store: bets, wallets, ledger, ticks) --------------------
# The ONE variable that switches the persistence driver. Unset → in-memory store
# (ephemeral, fine for tests/dev). Set → Postgres, used for everything that must
# survive a restart.
#
# Money moves use raw SQL transactions (SELECT … FOR UPDATE), so the game store
# talks Postgres directly over this connection string. supabase-js is reserved for
# auth admin (above).
#
# Supabase connection string formats — Project Settings → Database:
#   Session pooler (RECOMMENDED for the app; prepared statements work):
#     DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
#   Transaction pooler (PgBouncer; the driver auto-disables prepared statements):
#     DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
#   Direct (migrations + DDL such as scripts/partitions.ts):
#     DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:<password>@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres
DATABASE_URL=
